---
source: crates/trousseau-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Remove one or more recipients and re-encrypt the store.

SSH keys match on the key itself, so the trailing comment does not have to be the same. The last
recipient cannot be removed. Removing your own recipient asks for confirmation, because you lock
yourself out.

Usage: trousseau recipients rm [OPTIONS] <RECIPIENTS>...

Arguments:
  <RECIPIENTS>...
          The recipients to remove

Options:
      --force
          Skip the "you removed your own recipient" confirmation

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --store <PATH>
          Use this store file. Wins over `--global` and over store discovery
          
          [env: TROUSSEAU_STORE=]

      --global
          Use your personal store instead of the nearest project store (the `.trousseau` file in
          this directory or a parent)

      --identity <PATH>
          An identity (private key) file to try when unlocking. Repeatable. Also tried:
          `TROUSSEAU_IDENTITY_FILE`, the config file's `identity.files`, the default identity file,
          `~/.ssh/id_ed25519` and `~/.ssh/id_rsa`

      --passphrase-file <PATH>
          Read the store's passphrase from this file instead of prompting. One trailing newline is
          stripped

      --json
          Print one JSON document on stdout instead of text. Errors become a JSON object on stderr

      --quiet
          Suppress informational messages on stderr. Errors still print

      --no-input
          Never prompt. A command that would prompt fails instead: exit 4 for a secret, exit 2 for a
          confirmation

Examples:
  Remove a recipient:
    trousseau recipients rm age1...

  Remove your own recipient without the confirmation prompt:
    trousseau recipients rm --force age1...
